il card all draw it. The own figure is the summary's `cost.own.usd` (before it arrives, the day snapshot's `usd`); "with children" is `summary.cost.total`, which the item tool computes (`AICost.summary(AICost.session_url(id))`, one cached answer per session for every surface), never `SessionWork`'s own sum. The list never asks for every row: it shows an answer already here, else a small "with children …" button that asks for that one row. Clicking the Cost tile opens the Cost tab, whose first block lists every child session behind the total (`AICost.draw_session`). **The Overview tab is `SessionOutlineView.js` (+ `SessionOutline.css`, prefix `soutline-`), drawn from `SessionOutline.js`, which has no DOM and is tested by `node SessionOutline.test.mjs`.** It groups the session's work by child session: one box per child (name linking to that child's own page, state, model, an `AICost` cost line, "N of M done") holding the tasks whose folder is the child's or below it, then "This session's own work", sub-grouped by the prompt that asked for it (`SessionOutline.source(session)` is the one place that join lives) with "Other work" for the rest (today "Other work" still includes Prompt/Question chat records, each shown by its own words — a Prompt's cleaned paragraph, a Question's text, read by `constructor.name` since `type` is consumed picking the class — as a link to the Timeline tab, where that record has its own row; not counting them as tasks at all is open, held pending the owner's sign-off: [sessions/2026/10/25/session-5644835c/mastermind-session-page-tasks/requirements.md](../sessions/2026/10/25/session-5644835c/mastermind-session-page-tasks/requirements.md)). The children are the union, de-duplicated by session id, of the `sessions` lines of `session.jsonl`, the tree nodes that carry `session`, the day snapshot's `links.children`, and the snapshots whose `parent` is this session's agent; groups are ranked by cost × 0.5^(age days ÷ 2) plus recency, with a Cost/Newes